# Formula sheets → readiness checks

GitHub formula sheets are a US traffic source. Every public surface of `marfa77/cfa-frm-formula-sheets` carries this block, ahead of the deck links. Copy the same block into any new public gist or repo made from this dataset.

- CFA Level I: 60 questions, 90 minutes, free 25-question start — `https://uniprep2go.study/mock-exams/cfa-level-1-readiness-check`
- CFA Level II: 60 questions, 120 minutes, free 25-question start — `https://uniprep2go.study/mock-exams/cfa-level-2-readiness-check`
- FRM Part I: 50 questions, 120 minutes, free 25-question start — `https://uniprep2go.study/mock-exams/frm-part-1-readiness-check`

Surfaces: `README.template.md` (README is generated), `scripts/make_docs.py` output (`FORMULAS.md`, `docs/index.html`), `huggingface/README.md`. After a template or generator edit, run `python scripts/make_docs.py`.

Do not paste the block into an unrelated gist. The Cognitive Class Python notebook gist is not a formula sheet.

Do not republish PyPI, npm, or the Zenodo DOI just to add the links. If a package description is republished for another reason, include this block.
